{
  "_comment": "sc-18810 two-dimensional geometry sweep for mlx:ltx_2_3. Standalone, like the sc-18808 plan: generate-memory-matrix.mjs still resolves its coordinate universe from manifest.models.filter(m => m.type === \"image\"), so a video row in config/memory-calibration-plan.json matches no coordinate and reds the check gate (sc-18817 folds these in after sc-18815).\n\nDESIGN. Two spatial-latent levels (768x512 and 512x768 are 24x16 = 384 latent cells; 1280x704 and 704x1280 are 40x22 = 880) crossed with three frame levels per level, at a HELD-CONSTANT fps of 30. Crossing two AREAS is what makes the candidate forms separable at all: with one area the `mpx` column is proportional to the intercept, so BOTH the additive `perFrame` and the `perMpxFrame` cross designs are singular and neither coefficient is identifiable (pinned by scripts/fit-ltx-temporal-form.test.mjs). fps 30 is held because it is the only declared cadence whose duration ladder reaches the envelope maximum 449 (15 s x 30); every (frames, fps) pair here except the two noted below is a real declared durations x fps cell.\n\nRUNGS ARE NOT UNIFORM ACROSS THE ENVELOPE, which is why `rung` differs per entry. The LTX VAE decode auto-selects tiling, and the bound that binds first is machine-INDEPENDENT: `VaeTiling::LTX.writable_frame_cap(h, w) = i32::MAX / (8*h*w)` (gen-core/src/tiling.rs:166, full_res_channels 8) is 682 / 682 / 655 / 297 / 297 over the five declared resolutions, so only the two 0.90 MP buckets can reach it inside the 449-frame envelope, and they reach it at 298 output frames. Above it `budgeted_plan` tiles on every host. The `fit` and `held_out` points are therefore all rung-1 single-pass decodes, and the `rung2_boundary` points are rung 2 -- fitting one curve across that break would fit through a capability change.\n\nROLES. `fit` trains the candidate forms. `held_out` is never fitted: a third area (640x640, 400 latent cells) and both transposed aspect ratios. `held_out_fps_probe` re-renders an identical {w,h,frames} at 24 fps to measure the audio-latent axis GeometryEnvelope cannot express (LTX denoises audio latents jointly every step with length compute_audio_frames(frames, fps)). `rung2_boundary` brackets the tiling boundary at 1280x704: f297 is the cap exactly (a declared 10 s x 30 fps cell, single-pass) and f305 is one lattice step above it (off the declared duration ladder but on the engine's 1+8k lattice and inside the declared envelope), plus the envelope maximum f449 at every tier.\n\nDrive with: node scripts/memory-calibration-harness.mjs run --config docs/calibration/sc-18810/ltx-mlx-geometry-sweep.json --backend mlx --provider <name> --fresh-per-case --provider-command '[\"<target>/release/memory-mlx-adapter\"]' --sceneworks-repo <repo> --inference-repo <inference-at-pin> --resume <out.json> --output <out.json>, with --output OUTSIDE the repo, and SCENEWORKS_LTX_{REPOSITORY,REVISION,ROOT,TEXT_ENCODER_ROOT} set.",
